Rules:
- Make the preview specific to the client's business.
- Hero headline must be punchy and outcome-focused (e.g. "Turn Instagram DMs into booked appointments") — NEVER "Welcome to your custom X solution".
- Subheadline must explain the concrete value in one sentence.
- admin_dashboard_preview.cards must have realistic non-empty value fields (e.g. "12", "8", "34%") — never leave value empty.
- recent_activity must be specific and believable (e.g. "Sarah booked Botox consultation via Instagram").
- preview_content is REQUIRED — every field must match THIS client's industry and services (meal plans for a dietitian, NOT clinic treatments unless they are a clinic).
- app_config is REQUIRED — customize tabs, labels, enabled_modules, schedule_variant, and home_sections for THIS specific business. Omit modules they do not need (e.g. no schedule if they only need a client portal).
- Tab labels must use the business's language (Programs vs Treatments vs Features vs Menu).
- Choose schedule_variant progress for coaching/habit tracking; calendar for clinics, bookings, demos.
- feature_cards titles must become website.services names — same offerings, same language.
- inbox messages and conversations must reference the actual services from this business.
- schedule appointments and dashboard leads must use realistic client names and the business's actual offerings.
- image_theme: wellness for clinics/spas, fitness for coaches/dietitians/gyms, saas for software businesses, generic otherwise.
- Do not use Botox, Hydrafacial, or aesthetic clinic language unless the business is clearly a clinic or spa.
- Do not copy the reference brand or exact design.
- Do not mention that this is fake.
- Use realistic placeholder data.
- Make the concept look premium and useful.
- Keep all text client-facing and easy to understand.
- Use 3 to 6 feature cards.
- Use 3 to 5 user journey steps.
- Use 2 to 4 screen mockups.
- If the product needs an admin dashboard, set admin_dashboard_preview.should_show to true.
- If it does not need an admin dashboard, set admin_dashboard_preview.should_show to false.
- Never include dollar amounts, currency symbols, or numeric pricing in any text.